---
description: Block all git shell commands for the agent (no commit, push, pull, etc.)
alwaysApply: true
---

# No git shell commands

The agent must **never** run git remote-write commands in the terminal, including:

- `git push`, `git -C push`
- Any other `git` remote-write subcommand

The agent might run local git read commands without asking, but all write commands must be confirmed. Exceptions that must **never** be run (not even after confirmation prompts from the agent): `git push` and `git reset` (see `no-git-reset.mdc`).

If deployment or remote sync is needed, tell the user what to run — do not run it.
